---

### [box 12](box12)
---
Relic: ossuary
Box: -2266, 719, 6560, 1839, 775, 3176
---
A column running the height of the shaft. Vertical, so the plan shows it as a disc.

### [the vault door](vault_door)
---
Relic: ossuary
Point: 2682, 0, 2482
Roles: vault_door
---
What the reliquary is waiting for. `Roles:` on a point puts a real, invisible object here
when the relic is armed, and `Starts when: reach vault_door 900` measures against it - so
the Beacon appears the moment a ship comes within 900u of this spot, and not before.

### [the shaft floor](floor)
---
Relic: ossuary
Point: 0, 1600, 0
Item: power_cell
Qty: 3
---
No `Starts when:`, so this is simply there - the common case, and it needs no word.

### [the mouth](mouth)
---
Relic: ossuary
Point: -1500, 0, 0
Roles: entrance
---
The way in. A point adds no space of its own - it names a place, and the mission puts
something there: a navpoint the crew can steer to, and the spot they arrive at.

### [the reliquary](cache)
---
Relic: ossuary
Point: 4651, 0, 3188
Roles: item, quest
Item: red_beacon
Starts when: reach vault_door 900
---
Something worth the trip, at the far end. Authored RELATIVE to the relic's `Loc:`, so it
travels with the relic - which is why this is a relic part and not a landmark.
